      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-7);">The Story</h2>
      <p>I started in November 2019 on the remote-operations side of OKash Kenya, a fintech lender: scheduling social content, building performance reports, coordinating a virtual team spread across the city. The team part is what stuck. The process I built for tracking a distributed team's work is roughly the same one I still run today.</p>
      <p>M-KOPA is where the real foundation got built. Two years running CRM at scale for one of East Africa's best-known asset-finance platforms, keeping the data clean enough that senior management could actually use it, reworking ticket tracking until response times held up under volume. That job taught me the thing this whole career is built on: reliability comes from the system, not from working harder inside a broken one.</p>
      <p>Pioneer Outsourcing BPO is where it came together. I joined as Executive Partner to the CEO in January 2022, and over four years the remote agent workforce grew past 200, team response time dropped 80% after I rebuilt the workflows, and I wrote the SOP library the floor still runs on. I was promoted to Chief of Staff in April 2026.</p>
      <p>None of that happened one job at a time. For a year, Pioneer and MSTRpay's Kenya market entry ran side by side: I was Country Lead and Executive Partner to their Global CPO, coordinating joint-venture and capital-partnership talks with microfinance banks and development finance institutions, keeping a live pipeline of 20-plus partnerships visible at any hour. Right now I'm also Executive Administrator to the Group CEO of Auto Audit Group, running one calendar across the parent company and its subsidiaries Q360, Axios, and Dotify. Alongside that: ongoing work for Epena Law in the UK, where privilege rules govern every meeting note and decision log, Jivan Wellness in Kenya (part of the same Auto Audit Group), and Gregory Swarn Enterprises in the US, coordinating between Nairobi and US Eastern hours.</p>
      <p>Different employers, different titles: operations support, customer operations executive, executive partner, chief of staff, executive administrator. The job underneath barely moves. Every leader I've worked for has needed the same things: their time back, an execution rhythm, and systems that hold up when I'm not the one running them. That's why this site lists <a href="/hire-me/">eleven role names</a>. Companies search for the title their org chart uses. The work is one craft.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-7);">How I Work</h2>
      <p>Three principles, visible in every engagement. <strong>Visibility:</strong> every commitment tracked, every owner named. Dashboards replace inbox archaeology. <strong>Discipline:</strong> SLAs on response time, decisions logged, prep delivered 24 hours ahead. <strong>Async-first:</strong> documented processes and decision-ready summaries built for multi-time-zone teams. The full methodology is on <a href="/services/">the services page</a>; the receipts are in <a href="/case-studies/">the case studies</a> and <a href="/portfolio/">portfolio</a>.</p>

